{
  "category": "Magnet Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Formed by several MAGNEMITEs linked together. They frequently appear when sunspots flare up.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formed by several MAGNEMITEs linked together. They frequently appear when sunspots flare up.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Generates strange radio signals. It raises the tem perature by 3.6F degrees within 3,300 feet.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three MAGNEMITE are linked by a strong magnetic force. Earaches will occur if you get too close.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "The MAGNEMITE are united by a magnetism so power ful, it dries all moisture in its vicinities.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "When many MAGNETON gather together, the resulting magnetic storm disrupts radio waves.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "MAGNETON emits a powerful magnetic force that is fatal to mechanical devices. As a result, large cities sound sirens to warn citizens of large-scale outbreaks of this POKéMON.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "MAGNETON emits a powerful magnetic force that is fatal to electronics and precision instruments. Because of this, it is said that some towns warn people to keep this POKéMON inside a POKé BALL.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is actually three MAGNEMITE linked by magnetism. It generates powerful radio waves that raise temperatures by 3.6 degrees F within a 3,300-foot radius.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "A linked cluster formed of several MAGNEMITE. It discharges powerful magnetic waves at high voltage.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formed by several MAGNEMITE linked together. They frequently appear when sunspots flare up.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is actually three MAGNEMITE linked by magnetism. A group can set off a magnetic storm.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is actually three MAGNEMITE linked by magnetism. A group can set off a magnetic storm.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many mysteriously appear when more sunspots dot the sun. They stop TV sets from displaying properly.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three MAGNEMITE are linked by a strong magnetic force. Earaches will occur if you get too close.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "The MAGNEMITE are united by a magnetism so powerful, it dries all moisture in its vicinity.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many mysteriously appear when more sunspots dot the sun. They stop TV sets from displaying properly.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many mysteriously appear when more sunspots dot the sun. They stop TV sets from displaying properly.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stronger electromagnetic waves from the three linked Magnemite are enough to dry out surrounding moisture.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stronger electromagnetic waves from the three linked Magnemite are enough to dry out surrounding moisture.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "A linked cluster formed of several Magnemite. It discharges powerful magnetic waves at high voltage.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Generates strange radio signals. It raises the temperature by 3.6 degrees Fahrenheit within 3,300 feet.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magneton emits a powerful magnetic force that is fatal to mechanical devices. As a result, large cities sound sirens to warn citizens of large-scale outbreaks of this Pokémon.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magneton emits a powerful magnetic force that is fatal to electronics and precision instruments. Because of this, it is said that some towns warn people to keep this Pokémon inside a Poké Ball.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When three Magnemite link together, their brains also become one. They do not become three times more intelligent.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has about three times the electrical power of Magnemite. For some reason, outbreaks of this Pokémon happen when lots of sunspots appear.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Delicate equipment can malfunction in areas inhabited by Magneton, which send out mysterious electrical signals.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When rain clouds form, many Magneton gather in high places to wait for lightning to strike.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Generates strange radio signals. It raises the temperature by 3.6 degrees Fahrenheit within 3,300 feet.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Generates strange radio signals. It raises the temperature by 3.6 degrees Fahrenheit within 3,300 feet.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is three Magnemite that have linked together. Magneton sends out powerful radio waves to study its surroundings.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is constantly putting out a powerful magnetic force. Most computers go haywire when a Magneton approaches.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three Magnemite gathered to evolve into this Pokémon. The source of much vexation on my part, as its powerful magnetism destroys my research equipment.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
